## Answer

The file is: **`gson/src/main/java/com/google/gson/internal/bind/EnumTypeAdapter.java`**

This is the single file that builds the enum name-to-constant lookup used during enum deserialization. Specifically, the constructor of the `EnumTypeAdapter` class (lines 64-111) creates the `nameToConstant` HashMap that maps enum names to their constant values.

The bug is in the constructor's logic (lines 95-102):

```java
SerializedName annotation = constantField.getAnnotation(SerializedName.class);
if (annotation != null) {
  name = annotation.value();
  for (String alternate : annotation.alternate()) {
    nameToConstant.put(alternate, constant);  // Only adds alternates
  }
}
nameToConstant.put(name, constant);  // Adds the primary serialized name
```

When `@SerializedName` is present, the code overwrites the original enum constant name and only adds the alternate names and the primary serialized name to the lookup map. The original `constant.name()` value is lost and never added to `nameToConstant`, causing deserialization with alternate names to fail.
